there are those that agree with you.  let me explain my perspective
 ("no -dave-, don't explain, please???, oh foo")

in bizarro world, any device that gives more than 1 wish is a loophole.
for that reason, w.o.w.'s don't exist here.  the residents, naturally
wanting to wish now and then, have found varied alternate means of
doing this.  the bizzarons have a healthy respect for wishing because
they cannot hope to exploit multiple wishes.  the bizzarons have nothing
against wishing itself and do partake of it when it arises naturally.
for example, bizarrons are known to break bones (left behind after
monster kills) in the hope of finding a rare wishbone, and so on.

btw, there's this guy Aladdin who is a unique exception and cult hero
amongst bizarrons because he possesses "a ring of more wishes" and,
of course, _the_ lamp.  but even Aladdin is only capable of 3 wishes.
and besides, reaching Aladdin's place requires a quest of a 1,001
days and arabian nights.  few can hack it ...

